#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# apart

#% text
# `apart(e, x)` writes the rational function `e` of `x` as a sum of partial fractions.

#% text
# `apart(e)` does the same when `e` has one variable.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The result is a polynomial part plus fractions whose denominators are powers of the factors of the denominator of `e`.

#% item
# The denominator is factored over the rational numbers: a factor such as x^2 + 1 or x^2 - 2 stays whole.

#% item
# Other variables are treated as parameters.

#% item
# An expression that is not a rational function of `x` with exact coefficients is left unevaluated.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# Two simple fractions:

#% cell
apart(1/(x^2 - 1))
#% output
#= (-1/2)/(1 + x) + (1/2)/(-1 + x)

#% text
# A repeated factor of the denominator:

#% cell
apart(1/(x^2*(x + 1)))
#% output
#= -x^-1 + x^-2 + (1 + x)^-1

#% text
# A numerator of the same degree gives a polynomial part:

#% cell
apart((x^2 + 1)/(x^2 - 1))
#% output
#= 1 - (1 + x)^-1 + (-1 + x)^-1

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A square in the denominator:

#% cell
apart((3x + 5)/((x + 1)^2*(x - 2)))
#% output
#= (-11/9)/(1 + x) + (-2/3)*(1 + x)^-2 + (11/9)/(-2 + x)

#% text
# An irreducible quadratic factor stays whole:

#% cell
apart(1/(x^3 - 1), x)
#% output
#= (1/3)/(-1 + x) + (-2/3 + (-1/3)*x)/(1 + x + x^2)

#% cell
apart(1/(x^4 - 1))
#% output
#= (-1/2)/(1 + x^2) + (-1/4)/(1 + x) + (1/4)/(-1 + x)

#% text
# Symbolic parameters:

#% cell
apart(1/((x - a)*(x - b)), x)
#% output
#= (a - b)^-1/(x - a) + -1/(a - b)/(x - b)

#% text
# A rational function of several variables, split in `x`:

#% cell
apart(1/(x*y + y), x)
#% output
#= y^-1/(1 + x)

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# Integrate a rational function term by term:

#% cell
apart(1/(x*(x + 1)*(x + 2)))
#% output
#= -(1 + x)^-1 + (1/2)/x + (1/2)/(2 + x)

#% cell
integrate(apart(1/(x^2 - 1)), x)
#% output
#= (-1/2)*log(1 + x) + (1/2)*log(-1 + x)

#% text
# A telescoping sum: 1/(k(k + 1)) = 1/k - 1/(k + 1), so the sum up to n is 1 - 1/(n + 1):

#% cell
apart(1/(k*(k + 1)), k)
#% output
#= -(1 + k)^-1 + k^-1

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `together` undoes `apart`:

#% cell
together(apart((3x + 5)/((x + 1)^2*(x - 2))))
#% output
#= (5 + 3*x)/(-2 + -3*x + x^3)

#% cell
simplify(apart((3x + 5)/((x + 1)^2*(x - 2))) - (3x + 5)/((x + 1)^2*(x - 2)))
#% output
#= 0

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# Factors with irrational roots are not split:

#% cell
apart(1/(x^2 - 2))
#% output
#= (-2 + x^2)^-1

#% text
# Inexact coefficients are not handled:

#% cell
apart(1/(x^2 - 1.0))
#% output
#= apart((-1.0 + x^2)^-1)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `together`, `factor`, `cancel`, `integrate`, `polynomial_quotient`
